\deleted{$A'\times B_0\quad\unsure{A'\,h(i_0)}$}

We find
\[
i'\boxtimes(i=h(i_0,I,e))=h(i'\boxtimes i_0,I,e)
\]
\margin{\uline{check some}\ \uline{\unsure{day}}}
and the symmetric formula, so \unsure{we win}.

\uline{We do not know yet} M1 (factorization of any $f$ as $pi$, with either $i\in C,p\in TF$, or $i\in TC,p\in F$), nor M5 (saturation of $\widetilde W$ --- indeed we need only check a), b), to have a closed model category). The factorization $f=pi$ is the usual argument for constructing injectives, using reasonable properties of existence of \inserted{small} generating set of $\mathcal A$, and of filtering direct limits.
The lifting property may again be axiomatized in terms of $\unsure{\Phi^*},\Phi_*$, in a topos or a more general category --- I'll not for the moment work out this general formulation, and \deleted{be content} I'll assume the factorizability \deleted{\unsure{of $f$}} in the two ways.
\margin{\uline{to work}\ \uline{out}}

We now want to identify $\widetilde W$, and check condition b) of saturation. We want even prove $\widetilde W=W$ --- now it becomes essential to \deleted{\unsure{say}} make clear how the definition of $(TC)_0$ \uline{depends} on $W$, taking as ``bunch'' of \deleted{intervals} all intervals $I$ which are $W$-aspheric over $e$. But this may make a difficulty for factorization;
